From 8be305b3174438a49aa691871617abe6c10b156a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:35:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/26] Plugins: window sizes to switch between, set by the
 player

A plugin's window or the plugin dock could only be resized from its
edges, which a locked (click-through) window doesn't offer. Three
numbered buttons beside the text size, in the dock's panel bar and in a
plugin window's bar, switch the window between three sizes: a click
gives it the size kept under that button, a right-click (or Shift+click)
keeps the window's size now under it ("Size 2 is now 640 x 680"). The
dock has its own three (420 x 560, 640 x 680, 960 x 820 to begin with),
each plugin window its own; the button whose size the window has shows
pressed. They are buttons of those bars, so they stay clickable while
the windows are locked (patch 0007). The meter resizes the window
(plugin_window_size: the dock and plugin windows only, each only
itself, 240 x 120 to 2000 x 1600), and remembers the size as any other;
a folded dock unfolds first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RBQati3x8VviBbpY9juEWf
